            <ArticleTitle>Nonrecurring transient cortical blindness after coronary angiography: a role for hypoventilation and hypercarbia?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>384-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 73-year-old morbidly obese patient suffered cortical blindness following coronary angiography. Symptoms rapidly resolved and did not recur following a repeated procedure. Hypoventilation due to narcotics with subsequent hypercarbia and blood-brain barrier breaching may be implicated in the pathogenesis of this complication.</AbstractText>
